 :disagreements
 [{:topic "A slice that leaves the candidate unchanged"
   :raised-by [:workflow]
   :positions ["Legacy driver: it is a failure of the slice."
               "Continuation policy: it is a stall; stop continuing and move on."]}
  {:topic "Duplicate verdicts from one grader"
   :raised-by [:skeptic :instrument]
   :positions ["Skeptic: the duplicate is superseded (last one stands); only double counting must be prevented."
               "Instrument: last-wins is silent; a grader emitting duplicates should be refused."]}
  {:topic "Whether scoring tools are fenced from the clean room"
   :raised-by [:operator :instrument]
   :positions ["Fence them: the clean room holds no grading harness."
               "Leave them: the legacy siblings did not fence them. Both participants report it undecided."]}
  {:topic "What is pivotal inside the regenerate and gate phases"
   :raised-by [:workflow :skeptic :operator :instrument]
   :positions ["Workflow and skeptic: session resume, worker replacement and several refusals are pivotal; they protect the cycle's integrity."
               "Operator and instrument: only approvals, the gate verdict, the filed measurement and the conclusion split the timeline. Facilitator followed this reading."]}
  {:topic "Is the checklist a pivotal event"
   :raised-by [:instrument :operator]
   :positions ["Instrument: yes, it sets the denominator."
               "Operator: no, it is a policy reaction to the selection being approved."]}
  {:topic "Who issues the self-check and the receipt"
   :raised-by [:workflow :skeptic :operator]
   :positions ["Workflow: ORC stages do."
               "Operator and skeptic: the harness does. Glossary: ORC reports execution facts; the harness records stage facts, so both may be right at different layers."]}]}
